  "verdict": "allowed",
  "section": "27",
  "quote": "A landlord or, with the written authorization of a landlord, a broker or salesperson registered under the Trust in Real Estate Services Act, 2002, may enter a rental unit in accordance with written notice given to the tenant at least 24 hours before the time of entry to allow a potential purchaser to view the rental unit.",
  "reason": "Section 27(2) and (3) explicitly permit the landlord to enter the rental unit to allow a potential purchaser to view it, provided the landlord gives at least 24 hours written notice specifying the reason, day, and a time of entry between 8 a.m. and 8 p.m. The clause matches these exact statutory requirements."
}

